\description{
Saves \code{spec} as a non-self-contained HTML file and
returns a raw \verb{<iframe>} HTML block pointing at it.
Since formats like markdown and gfm
pass raw HTML through untouched, this embeds a genuinely live
widget even inside a plain-markdown document, as long as the
\emph{page it ends up on} is eventually served over http(s) rather
than opened as a local file.
(See \code{\link[=vg_snapshot]{vg_snapshot()}}'s Details for why \verb{file://} doesn't
work for a vgplotr widget).
